  "prefLabel": "Occ 102.05 Occupational therapy",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Occ 102.05 “Occupational therapy” means “occupational therapy” as defined in RSA 326-C:1, IV, namely “the care and services provided by an occupational therapist or occupational therapy assistant who are licensed pursuant to this chapter. Areas of occupation include but are not limited to:\n\n(a) Activities of daily living, which are the routine activities a person completes to meet their basic health and survival needs.\n\n(b) Instrumental activities of daily living, which are activities a person completes to live independently and participate in the community.\n\n(c) Health management.\n\n(d) Rest and sleep.\n\n(e) Education.\n\n(f) Work.\n\n(g) Play.\n\n(h) Leisure.\n\n(i) Social participation.”\n\nSource. #14366, eff 9-9-25 (from Occ 102.03)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/occ100-500.html"
